  "solution": "Given:\n\nA mobile is marked at a price 25% above its cost price.\n\nProfit = 5%\n\nFormula used:\n\nSP = (100 + Profit)/100 × C.P100+������100×��\" id=\"MathJax-Element-20-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">100+������100×��100+������100×��\" id=\"MathJax-Element-21-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">100+������100×��100+������100×��\" id=\"MathJax-Element-137-Frame\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\">100+������100×��100+������100×�� 100+������100×�� 100+������100×�� 100+������100×�� 100+������100×�� \n\nCalculations: \n\nLet the CP of the article be Rs. 100\n\nMP of the article = Rs. 125\n\nSP of the article = 100 × (105/100)\n\n= Rs. 105\n\nDiscount = 125 – 105 = 20\n\nDiscount percentage = 20/125 × 100 = 16%\n\nHence, the Discount percentage is 16%.\n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/661340121ece4245dffae37dda41ddab0ce1f2bf0ba4a0210bff82185deedb2e.png] __Shortcut Trick__\n\n5 = 25 – x – (25x/100)\n\n5 = 25 – x – x/4\n\n5x/4 = 20\n\nx = 16% \n\n104:T3a36,\n<p data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\" style=\"color: rgb(30, 43, 51); --darkreader-inline-color: #cecac4;",
